# Authors: Simon Davidson & Claude | Created 2026-08-25 | Last modified 2026-08-25
#
# tb_hu_compute with HU_II=1 AND randomised packer back-pressure.
#
# The pipeline handles pak_full_i by freezing every stage at once, so this is
# the test that matters most for it: a write stalling while a multiply result
# lands is exactly the hazard a global freeze exists to prevent. The Monarch
# workload never back-pressures (HU_PROFILE measured the packer never full),
# so without this the path would ship unexercised.
xrun -sv -timescale 1ns/1ps -access wrc -top tb_hu_compute \
  -define HU_II -define HU_BP \
  hu_compute.v tb_hu_compute.v
